# SLOW COOKER WHITE CHICKEN CHILI
## info
* About 20 minutes prep, 4 to 6 hours cooking
* 6 to 8 servings

## ingredients
* 3 tablespoons unsalted butter
* 1 large yellow or red onion, finely chopped
* kosher salt
* 10 garlic cloves, finely chopped
* 1 jalapeño, minced
* 3 (4-ounce) cans chopped green chiles
* 2 teaspoons ground cumin
* 2 teaspoons onion powder
* 1 teaspoon dried oregano
* 1/2 teaspoon ground cayenne
* 2 pounds boneless, skinless chicken thighs
* 3 cups chicken stock
* 2 (14-ounce) cans great Northern beans, drained and rinsed
* 1 1/2 cups frozen corn
* 1 cup finely chopped fresh cilantro (optional)
* juice of 1 lime (about 2 tablespoons)

### optional toppings
* pickled jalapeño slices
* sliced scallions
* cubed avocado
* sour cream

## steps
1. Melt the butter in a large Dutch oven over medium heat. Add the onion, season with salt, and cook until softened and translucent, about 8 minutes.
1. Add the garlic and jalapeño and cook for 1 minute until fragrant.
1. Stir in the green chiles, cumin, onion powder, oregano, and cayenne. Cook for 1 to 2 minutes until fragrant.
1. Transfer the mixture to a 5- to 8-quart slow cooker.
